WEBVTT

00:04:57.541 --> 00:05:00.162
from very, very small things
to very, very big things.

00:05:00.186 --> 00:05:02.560
You have to try very hard
to get outside of this.

00:05:02.584 --> 00:05:06.385
And there is also a frontier
in research physics here,

00:05:06.409 --> 00:05:08.212
it's just that nobody talks about it.

00:05:08.236 --> 00:05:09.913
This is the world of the complex.

00:05:09.937 --> 00:05:12.184
When these laws work together,
they bring about

00:05:12.208 --> 00:05:15.038
the beautiful, messy,
complex world we live in.

00:05:15.062 --> 00:05:18.735
Fundamentally, this is the bit
that really matters to me

00:05:18.759 --> 00:05:19.949
on an everyday basis.

00:05:19.973 --> 00:05:22.152
And this is the bit
that we don't talk about.

00:05:22.176 --> 00:05:24.510
There's plenty of physics
research going on here.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.908
But because it doesn't involve
pointing at stars,

00:05:26.932 --> 00:05:29.014
people for some reason
think it's not that.

00:05:29.038 --> 00:05:32.520
Now, the cool thing about this
is that there are so many things